{"tool_name":"objtables","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"objtables","home":"https://www.objtables.org","license":"MIT","summary":"ObjTables is a toolkit for creating re-usable datasets that are both human and machine-readable, combining the ease of spreadsheets (e.g., Excel workbooks) with the rigor of schemas (classes, their attributes, the type of each attribute, and the possible relationships between instances of classes).\n\nObjTables consists of a format for describing schemas for spreadsheets, numerous data types for science, a syntax for indicating the class and attribute represented by each table and column in a workbook, and software for using schemas to rigorously validate, merge, split, compare, and revision datasets.\n\nObjTables is ideal for supplementary materials of journal article, as well as for emerging domains which need to quickly build new formats for new types of data and associated software with minimal effort.","addition_date":"2020-05-22T16:38:49Z","last_update_date":"2021-04-26T08:31:13Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library","Web API","Web application"],"version":["1.0.0"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:objtables","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"karr@mssm.edu","name":"Jonathan Karr","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2605-5080","typeEntity":"Person","url":"https://www.karrlab.org"}],"documentation":[{"type":["API documentation"],"url":"https://docs.karrlab.org/obj_tables"},{"type":["API documentation"],"url":"https://www.objtables.org/api"},{"type":["Training material"],"url":"http://sandbox.karrlab.org/tree/obj_tables"},{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://www.objtables.org/help"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"group"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Text data","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2526"},"format":[{"term":"CSV","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3752"},{"term":"JSON","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3464"},{"term":